    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29685" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῠωδεκᾱΐς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>, 
			Att.
		; 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δωδεκηΐς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῠωδεκα-ῄς</span></b> , -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῇδος, ἡ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sacrifice of twelve victims</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				2438
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>D</u>
				37
			</span></i> (Delph.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				3604.9
			</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Abst.</u>
				1.22
			</span></i>, etc.: as Adj., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυσίαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eust.
					1386.48
				</span></i>
			: hence name of a sacred mission to Delphi, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				773.2
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B.C.)</span>.</div>
